A||||8||ToddAsh||Alarm System Recommendations||||12||
Z||000000||ToddAsh||11-14-2000||05:37 PM||||Can anyone recommend a system for my Fiero? I put a Crimestopper 533i in my Jeep but wondered if any were easier or cheaper. The Crimestopper was $130. from Crutchfield. Thanks, Todd||||reg||12
Z||000001||Seanh||11-14-2000||05:58 PM||||Depends what features you want. I have a FirstTech Compustar 2K in mine. I have the web site but seem to have forgotten it off hand. It has about like 10 channels. What I did it Remote Start, window roll up, window roll down, lock and unlock doors, secitity system w/4 zones, light under car neon, trunk pop. It was $350.00 in the box, plus extras. It is $599 installed. Great system, youll see what I mean when I can find the website.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif"> <BR>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"If you smoke after sex, you're doing it way to fast".</I>||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||11-15-2000||08:44 AM||||I have an Alpine SEA-8081. was kinda pricey but has 2 way communication.. can tell which windo is open and will close the windows at the push of a button up to 1 mile away (or 1/4 mile and in the mall) was $588 installed. I'd like to have the remote start hooked up too. (for those COLD mornings)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||11-15-2000||09:51 AM||||I have a Chapman in mine. I installed it when I bought the car and have not had a problem yet. I would suggest that whichever brand you choose, That you go to a reputable place. I had an alarm system in my first Fiero that was installed by the place I bought it from and a week later I had to hit the brakes hard to avoid another car. Well the alarm brainbox slid out from under the dash and got wrapped around my feet.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR>Another helpful hit is most shops have a specific location where they install the brainbox. Which means if a car theif wants your car, he knows where the shop puts them too. After the above incident I have alwys done my own installs.||||reg||1
Z||000004||GodSend||11-15-2000||12:20 PM||||  I bought a clifford Nova LE - Should cost you less then 150 bucks.  It comes with shock sensor, light flasher, power lock (lock and unlock) , led (you can add another one and have two) and power trunk release and door sensors.<P>  It was pretty easy to install, and the brain is super small (about the size of a wallet .. so you can hide it anywhere).  You can buy extra relays (about 10 bucks each) to do the starter kill and other various features.... So its nice if you want to start off in the mid-level alarm area and then add some advanced features later..||||reg||14
Z||000005||deceler8||11-15-2000||02:01 PM||||I've had the same voltage sensing alarm now for the last 13 years (a Serpico...don't know if they're made anymore)...<P>One wire hookup, with two remotes to activate...very sensitive...<P>Opening any of the doors/trunk/hood sets it off as the "ajar" function sets off the current sensor. I've had thunder set off the vibration sensor and set it off yesterday just brushing snow off the car.<P>Cost about $100 back in 1988...other makes are even cheaper now.<P>Incredibly easy to install...a one piece unit that also includes the motion sensor and siren. About 3" by 4".||||reg||1
Z||000006||Seanh||11-15-2000||05:01 PM||||Mine is 2-way comunication also. If you can afford the extra money, get it. It is a great feature to have. Mine will work about 1 mile away. Having 2-way comunication, when you push a button on the remote to send a signal to the car, the in-car unit sends a signal back to the remote confirming the action. It also works as a pager if your system is set off.||||reg||1
Z||000007||overlord||11-15-2000||11:03 PM||||i picked  mine up for $50 canadian.<BR>It has dual-stage shock sensor, led, electrical disturbance detector (comes on if any power is drawn from battery or backup battery), two remotes, starter disable, and hooks up fiarly easy and twas cheap. It only goes to 120 DB, but for the price i am very  happy wityh it.<BR>Radio shack special.  -)||||reg||1
Z||000008||Seanh||11-15-2000||11:07 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.compustar.org" TARGET=_blank>www.compustar.org</A>  is the address. Its really worth looking into. ||||reg||1
